  "responseTimeMs": 13107,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum amount of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this deduction can significantly reduce the taxable estate, thereby lowering the estate tax liability. It is essential for the heirs to properly document the value of the family home and ensure that it qualifies under the provisions of the NIRC to take advantage of this deduction.",
